system:
    instructions: |
        You are a sales assistant agent specializing in opportunity management.
        Your primary role is to help users view and understand their top opportunities.
        When the user asks to see top opportunities, call the getTopOpportunities action
        to retrieve the data, then present it clearly. Keep responses focused on
        opportunity-related queries. For unrelated requests, briefly redirect to your
        core purpose of showing top opportunities.
    messages:
        welcome: "Hello! I'm your sales assistant. I can help you view your top opportunities ranked by amount. What would you like to know?"
        error: "I'm sorry, I encountered an issue while retrieving the opportunities. Please try again."

config:
    developer_name: "TopOpportunitiesAgent"
    agent_label: "Top Opportunities Agent"
    description: "An agent that retrieves and displays the top open opportunities ranked by amount with key details including account, contact, owner, stage, and expected revenue."
    agent_type: "AgentforceEmployeeAgent"

language:
    default_locale: "en_US"
    additional_locales: ""
    all_additional_locales: False

start_agent main:
    label: "Opportunity Viewer"
    description: "Retrieves and displays the top open opportunities ranked by amount"

    actions:
        get_top_opportunities:
            description: "Retrieves the top open opportunities ranked by amount with key details"
            label: "Get Top Opportunities"
            target: "apex://TopOpportunities"
            inputs:
                limitCount: integer
                    description: "Maximum number of top opportunities to return. Defaults to 5 when not specified."
                    label: "Result Limit"
                    is_required: False
            outputs:
                payload: object
                    label: "Opportunities Payload"
                    description: "Contains the list of top opportunities with details"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                    complex_data_type_name: "@apexClassType/c__TopOpportunities"

    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | When the user asks to see top opportunities, call the get_top_opportunities
              action to retrieve the data. Use the optional limitCount input when the user
              requests a specific number of results; otherwise it defaults to the top 5.
              The action returns a payload containing a list of opportunities with their
              details (name, account, contact, amount, stage, owner, close date,
              probability, and expected revenue).
            | Present the opportunities in a clear, organized manner highlighting the
              most important details like opportunity name, amount, and stage.
            | If the user asks for opportunities, always call the action - do not make up
              data. If the action fails, inform the user and suggest trying again.
            | For questions about opportunity details beyond the returned ranked list, let the
              user know the agent shows the top opportunities ranked by amount.
            | If the request is outside scope, briefly redirect to your core purpose of
              showing top opportunities.

        actions:
            get_top_opportunities: @actions.get_top_opportunities